t has been much better against the pass than the run, ranking 9th and 26th. Nik Bonitto has been as productive as expected, but the bigger surprise is Malcolm Roach, who has 3.5 sacks despite playing only 55% of the snaps. Their scheme has been fairly conventional, and the closest thing to a signature is an eight man box rate that ranks 13th highest in the league.","special":"The Broncos have been about average in how often they go for it on fourth down. Their kickers have made 82% of field goals, which is about average. Their salary cap was spread across positions in a fairly typical way. Their offensive line was among the oldest in the league.","players":"Bo Nix has played nearly every snap at quarterback and thrown for 1,493 yards. Jaylen Waddle has been the clear top target with 23% of the looks and 315 receiving yards. J.K. Dobbins has handled most of the work in the backfield with 57% of the carries. On defense, Zach Allen leads the team with 4.5 sacks and Brandon Jones has picked off 2 passes.","coaching":"Davis Webb is calling the offense and Vance Joseph is calling the defense. Their offense looks most like the 2022 Jaguars and the 2022 Patriots. Their defense looks most like the 2025 Patriots and the 2025 Colts under Lou Anarumo.","trends":"The offense went from 10th in EPA per play in 2025 to 20th so far this season, a big step back. The defense moved from 6th in EPA allowed per play in 2025 to 13th so far this season, a modest decline. The biggest change in approach was pre-snap motion rate, which went from 47% to 63%.","notes":"The 2026 pages are built from data that nflverse updates every week, so they will keep changing until the season ends. Personnel, formations, coverage and pressure numbers are missing for now because that data is only released after the season."}}